s albimanus </italic>in El Salvador. 3. Field methods and population control</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1974</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>288</fpage><lpage>297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4817674</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Curtis</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Louis C, Knols BGJ</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Review of previous applications of genetics to vector control</article-title><source>Bridging laboratory and field research for genetic control of disease vectors</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Dordrecht: Springer</publisher-name><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>43</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lowe</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Dame</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Savage</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaiser</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Efficiency of techniques for the mass release of sterile male <italic>Anopheles albimanus </italic>Wiedemann in El Salvador</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1980</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>695</fpage><lpage>703</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7406117</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dame</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lowe</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Williamson</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Kitzmiller B, Kanda T</surname></name></person-group>